Given a string, determine the maximum number of palindromic substrings that can be formed by rearranging the characters of the string. A palindromic substring is a string that reads the same backward as forward.

The function should take a string as input and return an integer representing the maximum number of palindromic substrings.

To solve this, first count the frequency of each character in the string. Then count how many distinct characters have an even frequency and how many have an odd frequency. If there is more than one character with an odd frequency, return 0. Otherwise, return the number of distinct characters with even frequency plus one if there is at least one character with an odd frequency.

